						Yukawa is the classical theoretical root of short-range strong binding. See <a href="/foundations/gell-mann-quarks-and-the-strong-interaction" class="text-white/80 underline decoration-white/25 underline-offset-4 transition hover:text-white hover:decoration-white/50">Gell-Mann</a> for the quark and colour refinement, <a href="/blog/particles-of-identity" class="text-white/80 underline decoration-white/25 underline-offset-4 transition hover:text-white hover:decoration-white/50">Particles of Identity</a> for the Strong Binding proposal, and <a href="/foundations/newton-absolute-space-and-forces" class="text-white/80 underline decoration-white/25 underline-offset-4 transition hover:text-white hover:decoration-white/50">Newton</a> for the earlier long-range force language.
					</p>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>

